# house.rules - the rule book: which steps run, in which mode, and what is relaxed where.
#
# Each line: layer | match | key | mode
#   layer  house, area, family, package or submission (in that order: the highest layer that matches
#          decides; inside a layer the last line decides)
#   match  * for every package; else the area (packages), the family (alchemy_website_publisher) or
#          the package directory (alchemy_website_publisher_v0.4)
#   key    a step id (mode enforce, report or off), STEP.RULE (mode off or warn), or FILES.EXCLUDE
#          (mode: path prefixes, separated by blanks, that no step reads)
# A relaxation belongs in the layer it applies to, with a comment saying why, so the receipt that cites
# it can be read back to a reason.
#
# Architecture: Tom Dyer. Written by: Claude (Opus 5.5), 2026-11-11.

# shadow mode: the workflow runs beside the Python Autobuild and stops nothing yet
house   | *  | Manifest     | report
house   | *  | HouseRules   | report
house   | *  | ModuleStamp  | report
house   | *  | KitRun       | report

# the module stamps are new (REQ-00003463, 11 Nov 2026): a missing stamp warns until the coordinator
# announces the rule; a wrong stamp is still a defect
house   | *  | ModuleStamp.MS-MISSING | warn

# test helpers are not components
house   | *  | FILES.EXCLUDE | tests/fixtures/

# the workflow judges itself at full strength
package | alchemy_workflow_v0.1-dev1 | Manifest    | enforce
package | alchemy_workflow_v0.1-dev1 | HouseRules  | enforce
package | alchemy_workflow_v0.1-dev1 | ModuleStamp | enforce
package | alchemy_workflow_v0.1-dev1 | ModuleStamp.MS-MISSING | enforce
package | alchemy_workflow_v0.1-dev1 | FILES.EXCLUDE | tests/
